#### 23. Toggle User Active Status

Activate or deactivate a user account. Deactivated users cannot log in.

```http
PATCH /api/admin/users/{user_id}/toggle-active
Authorization: Bearer {admin_token}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "is_active": false
}
```

**Path Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `user_id` | int | Yes | User ID |

**Request Body:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `is_active` | boolean | Yes | `true` to activate, `false` to deactivate |

**Response (200 - Deactivated):**
```json
{
    "status": "success",
    "message": "User has been deactivated",
    "data": {
        "id": 797,
        "firstname": "Driver",
        "lastname": "Test",
        "email": "driver@gmail.com",
        "is_active": false
    }
}
```

**Response (200 - Activated):**
```json
{
    "status": "success",
    "message": "User has been activated",
    "data": {
        "id": 797,
        "firstname": "Driver",
        "lastname": "Test",
        "email": "driver@gmail.com",
        "is_active": true
    }
}
```

**Error (400 - Bad Request):**
```json
{
    "status": false,
    "message": "is_active field is required and must be a boolean"
}
```

**Error (404 - Not Found):**
```json
{
    "status": false,
    "message": "User not found"
}
```

> **Note:** When a user is deactivated (`is_active = false`), their login attempts will return: `"Your account has been deactivated. Please contact the administrator."` with HTTP 403. Existing JWT tokens will also be blocked by the middleware.

